{
  "name": "Generate From Scene Cast (fbTools)",
  "_setup_notes": "Built from a real, working export: templates/minimax_h3_r2v_composition.api.json in the comfyui-fbTools repo (exported from the user's own video_minimax_h3_r2v_prompt_upscale.json workflow, 2026-10-02). fbt_CompositionLoad (3923) and fbt_PromptCompositionLoader (3924) BOTH have their composition_name wired to the __openshot_input:composition_name__ placeholder -- 3924's own value is semantically ignored at runtime once prompt_composition is wired (which it always is here), but it is still a COMBO input ComfyUI validates server-side by list-membership before execution ever starts; leaving it as an empty string (or any name not in the live composition list) makes ComfyUI reject the whole output chain with 'Value not in list' and silently produce nothing (confirmed 2026-10-02: 0.17s 'completion', zero real output). Wiring it to the same placeholder as 3923 keeps it always valid, since it mirrors whatever real composition the user picked. fbt_SceneCastBuild's cast_entries_json/composition_overrides_json are also OpenShot placeholders. The final VHS_VideoCombine (node 3927) was switched from the source workflow's image/gif@8fps preview setting to a real video/h264-mp4@24fps output with save_metadata on (required for OpenShot's embedded-metadata pre-fill to work on clips this template produces). Everything else -- model/checkpoint names, LoRA stack, sampler/scheduler settings, resolution/frame-count defaults -- is copied unchanged from the user's own tuned production workflow. This field is ignored by OpenShot/ComfyUI; it's just a note for future-you.",
  "menu_category": "enhance",
  "menu_order": 90,
  "action_icon": "ai-action-restyle.svg",
  "output_type": "video",
  "template_id": "video-scene-cast-generate",
